  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- guide
  "guide.rail": ["The steps in order, from checking the files to a robot that drives straight.",
    "Each step trusts the ones before it. ✓ Done means every target was met on the real robot; steering on blocks only needs 80 out of 100, because the floor finishes it.", null],
  "guide.step.connect": ["Connects and reads every robot file for numbers that don't add up.", "Most swerve problems are a wrong number in a file, and finding one costs nothing.", "gear_ratio"],
  "guide.step.health": ["Records 3 seconds standing still and checks every sensor is quiet.", "A noisy encoder or a drifting gyro makes every later measurement wrong.", "absolute_encoder"],
  "guide.step.hand": ["You turn wheels and modules by hand while the tool checks each sensor counts the right way.", "One backwards sign makes a module run away, and it looks like a tuning problem.", "hand_check"],
  "guide.step.offsets": ["Records each module's encoder while its wheel points exactly straight.", "One degree off drifts the robot about 1.7 cm sideways for every meter.", "offset"],
  "guide.step.directions": ["Spins each wheel slowly in the air so you can watch it roll forward.", "A backwards wheel fights the other three and drags the robot sideways.", "inversion"],
  "guide.step.steer-blocks": ["Tunes how fast and exactly each wheel turns to its angle, in the air.", "Nothing grips the wheel in the air, so it's the easy place to get the loop stable first.", "step_response"],
  "guide.step.geometry": ["Measures module spacing with a tape and the real wheel size with a push.", "Odometry turns wheel turns into meters, so a wrong wheel size makes every distance wrong.", "wheel_size"],
  "guide.step.steer-floor": ["Finishes steering on carpet; the wheels turn in place and the robot stays put.", "Carpet grips a turning wheel, so gains tuned in the air usually stop a few degrees short.", "carpet_scrub"],
  "guide.step.slip": ["Pushes the bumper into a wall, raising current until each wheel slips.", "Current past the slip point only spins the wheels, so the limit belongs just below it.", "slip_current"],
  "guide.step.ff": ["Drives forward and back to measure the volts each wheel needs to start, cruise and speed up.", "With that guess right, PID only has small errors left to fix.", "feedforward"],
  "guide.step.drive": ["Tunes how well each wheel holds the speed it's told.", "Feedforward does most of the work, so this PID can stay gentle and quiet.", "feedback"],
  "guide.step.spin": ["Spins in place both ways and compares the command, the gyro and the wheels.", "It catches a backwards gyro or module positions typed in wrong.", "gyro"],
  "guide.step.straight": ["Drives straight with no heading help and measures how far off it ends.", "With nothing correcting it, any drift is the drivetrain itself.", "offset"],
  "guide.step.profile": ["Lessons on smooth planned moves; unlocks when steering and drive pass on the floor.", "A profile only helps once the basic tuning already works.", "motion_profile"],
  "guide.step.commit": ["Saves the tuned numbers to files, redeploys, and commits them to git.", "Live changes vanish at restart; only committed files are the team's real settings.", "redeploy"],
  "guide.where": ["Where the robot must be for this step, and whether it is there now.",
    "On blocks the wheels spin in the air; on the floor the robot really drives. The safety rules differ, so the tool checks before anything moves.", "environment"],
  "guide.next": ["Opens the next step.", "It appears once this step is done.", null],
  "guide.config": ["Opens the list of numbers in the robot's files that don't add up.", "Red items break later steps, so fix them first; yellow ones are worth a look.", "gear_ratio"],
  "guide.run": ["Runs this step's test on the robot and shows what it found.", "Some steps tick from the run itself; others from what you confirm afterwards (the step says which).", "environment"],
  "guide.tune": ["Opens the Tune tab on this step's test.", "Run, read the advice, try the one change it suggests, and run again until every target is met.", "step_response"],
  "guide.hw": ["Records 20 seconds while you roll each wheel forward by hand.", "The motors coast so they turn freely; roll one way only, or the result reads AMBIGUOUS.", "coast_mode"],
  "guide.hs": ["Records 20 seconds while you turn each module counter-clockwise by hand.", "It checks both steering sensors count the same way, and that the steering gear ratio is right.", "coast_mode"],
  "guide.verdict": ["Whether each sensor counted the way the code expects.",
    "AGREES: right. INVERTED: flip that setting. NO_MOTION: turn it further or check its cable. AMBIGUOUS: move it one way only.", "inversion"],
  "guide.off": ["Averages 4 seconds of readings to find each wheel's straight-ahead number.", "If a wheel is bumped while it records, the tool asks you to capture again.", "hold_still"],
  "guide.ver": ["Checks every wheel now reads within 2° of straight.", "The robot loads new offsets only when its code restarts, so redeploy first.", "redeploy"],
  "guide.dir": ["Tick each wheel you saw roll forward (FL front-left, FR front-right, BL back-left, BR back-right).", "Any empty box opens the fix in Troubleshoot.", "inversion"],
  "guide.dirok": ["Records which wheels rolled forward.", "All four ticked passes the step.", null],
  "guide.calibrate": ["Opens the Calibrate tab, where the measuring tools are.", "Measure module positions and wheel sizes there, then come back.", null],
  "guide.mark": ["Records that you finished this step.", "The tool can't see your tape measure or your git commit, so you tell it.", null],

